#
# VISIONFIVE2 -- kernel configuration for the StarFive VisionFive 2 (JH7110).
#
# The product kernel. Until now this board was built as stock GENERIC, which
# meant the kernel a release shipped was implied by whatever files.starfive
# happened to contain rather than stated anywhere. This file is the statement.
#
# It deliberately starts from GENERIC rather than replacing it: GENERIC is
# maintained upstream and tracks changes we would otherwise have to chase by
# hand, and every driver this board needs already reaches it through
# std.starfive. What belongs here is what is true of the *product* and not of
# the architecture.

include		GENERIC

ident		VISIONFIVE2

#
# Not trimmed, on purpose.
#
# GENERIC also carries std.allwinner, std.cvitek, std.eswin and std.sifive,
# and builds the full module set. A product kernel would reasonably drop the
# other SoC vendors and use MODULES_OVERRIDE to build only what this board
# loads -- a real saving in build time and image size.
#
# That is not done here because it cannot be done safely by inspection: the
# board loads modules from three places (the kernel's own directory, the
# packages in /boot/modules, and whatever a compositor pulls in), and a list
# that looks complete until something is missed produces a board that boots
# and then fails in a way that looks like a driver bug. It is tracked as its
# own item so it gets the A/B it needs rather than being smuggled in here.
#
# The drivers this board actually depends on all arrive through
# std.starfive -> files.starfive:
#
#   jh7110_axidma     DesignWare AXI DMAC; audio cannot be paced without it
#   jh7110_pwmdac     3.5 mm jack, and its codec
#   jh7110_i2s        I2S TX0, the HDMI audio CPU DAI
#   jh7110_hdmi_audio HDMI audio codec
#   jh7110_inno_hdmi  HDMI transmitter
#   jh7110_gpio, _pmu, _rtc, _temp, _wdt, _pcie, starfive_syscon
#   wave5             Wave511 video decoder (module: /dev/video0)
#   sifive_ccache     needed for the L2 bypass alias the DMA paths rely on
#
# The GPU is not here: pvrsrvkm and the DRM modules are out-of-tree and come
# from graphics/pvrsrvkm-kmod and graphics/drm-vf2-kmod.
